.TH SDL_IOprintf 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_IOprintf \- Print to an
.BR SDL_IOStream
data stream.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_IOprintf(SDL_IOStream *context, const char *fmt, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function does formatted printing to the stream\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I context
a pointer to an
.BR SDL_IOStream
structure\[char46]
.TP
.I fmt
a printf() style format string\[char46]
.TP
.I ...
additional parameters matching % tokens in the
.BR fmt
string, if any\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes written or 0 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Do not use the same
.BR SDL_IOStream
from two threads at once\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_IOvprintf (3),
.BR SDL_WriteIO (3)
